'''Gistaín''' ({{Langx|mxi|خِسْتَإِينْ|H̱istaín}}), also spelled '''Chistén''', is a formerly industrial [[Communes of Balisca|barrio]] in the [[Charxes]] borough of the [[Castejón Metropolis]]. During the {{W|Industrial Revolution}} Gistaín emerged as a center of Baliscan industry. Surrounding the developing cluster of factories stood hastily built [[W:Company towns|company towns]]. When the industrial buzz passed, it entered a long {{W|urban decay|period of decay}}, and was later devastated by the [[1924 Alpujarra earthquake]]. 

The completion of [[Campo Nuevo]] and it's surrounding park was the main impetus for the revitalization of Gistaín. The [[Casajuan Plan]] aims to reconstruct and redevelop [[W:Deindustrialization|formerly industrial]] land Gistaín into a new residential housing estates, as well as to increase leisure and residential spaces. Alongside the newly built [[Alfafar]] and [[Foro]] ("forum") districts, art and design studios and associated artists and young [[W:Bohemianism|bohemians]] have converted the former factories and warehouses into lofts, galleries, and shops, making the area known for its creative outlook. 

